config ENABLE_TUYA_PM
    bool "Enable power-level manager (tuya_pm)"
    default n
    select ENABLE_WIFI_ULTRA_LOWPOWER if ENABLE_WIFI
    help
      Device power-level manager: a policy/arbitration layer that maps discrete
      power levels (ACTIVE/STANDBY/DORMANT/DEEPSLEEP) onto lpmgr / tal_cpu
      wakelock / tdl_power / tkl_wakeup. Products declare a policy and register
      hold-locks / consumers; the manager arbitrates the effective level and
      decays on idle.

      On WiFi platforms this pulls in the WiFi ULP framework (lpmgr) as the deep
      low-power backend, so the online levels can actually reach uA.

